Visualizar > Som dos Vídeos ao Abrir: videos start with sound on, off, or as the app decides

The choice is sent to the app as a phone sends it, through the volume rocker,
never through the app's internals:
- on: music volume up one step, then KEYCODE_VOLUME_UP;
- off: music volume to 0, then KEYCODE_VOLUME_DOWN; the volume is put back
  quietly once the key is handled. (Instagram reads "volume down with the stream
  at 0" as sound off and "volume up" as sound on, for the feed and for Reels.)
It is sent when a track starts playing (AudioTrack.play): a video is on screen
and the controller that owns it is the one listening for the key. Instagram's
feed takes the key only while a feed video plays, so a try that nobody takes is
repeated on a later track (3 s apart, at most 6 tries). Under "off" the track that
carries the try is held silent until the app's player has applied its new
volume, so the first video never blips at full sound.

AudioManager now behaves like a volume an app can watch: the stream volumes are
shared, setStreamVolume/adjustStreamVolume notify content://settings/system and
broadcast VOLUME_CHANGED_ACTION with its extras.

Native side (cocoa_bridge.mm): the menu section with three choices (Ativado,
Desativado, Padrão do Instagram), kept in the user defaults (VideoSoundAtStart),
copied before the JVM starts into MACAPK_VIDEO_SOUND_AT_START (which still wins
when set) by a constructor, and sent to AudioManager.macapkSetVideoSoundAtStart at
once when changed from the menu. MACAPK_AUDIO_VOLUME_TRACE=1 logs every
AudioTrack.setVolume with its caller.

